## Section 1-India-Specific Keyword Research Outline

Keyword research for Indian medical practices requires a different approach than generic global guides suggest. Patient search behavior in India is shaped by language preferences, city-level targeting, and the rapid rise of telehealth.

### High-Intent Transactional Keywords (Exact + Phrase Match Only)

- "best [specialty] in [city]"-e.g., best cardiologist in Delhi, best skin doctor in Bangalore
- "[specialty] near me"-universal, high-intent across all cities
- "book appointment [specialty] [city]"-direct booking intent
- "[specialty] doctor fees [city]"-price-conscious but booking-ready patients
- "online consultation [specialty]"-telehealth boom post-COVID, rising 40% YoY

### India-Specific Negative Keywords-Add From Day One

**Irrelevant searches waste 30–40% of medical ad budgets. Build this negative list before launch:**

> "free," "MBBS fees," "medical college admission," "doctor salary," "government hospital," "AIIMS," "how to become," "jobs," "internship," "case study," "symptoms only," "home remedy," "Ayurveda" (if running allopathy ads)

### Regional Language Keywords-Untapped Opportunity

No competitor in this space is targeting Hindi or regional language searches-which represent a significant and growing patient segment in Tier 2 and Tier 3 Indian cities. Consider campaign layers for:

- Hindi searches: "paas mein doctor," "dil ka doctor Delhi mein"
- Tamil, Telugu, Kannada, Marathi variants for respective state capitals
- Use Google's language targeting settings to serve regional ads to regional language users

## Section 2-Campaign Structure Outline

One campaign per major service line, and one ad group for each specific service or medical condition within that line-never mix different intents or specialties in a single campaign. This structured approach improves ad relevance, Quality Score, and conversion rates. With professional [Google Ads Management Services](https://www.clickbriz.com/google-ads-management-services), healthcare providers can build well-organized campaigns that deliver better targeting, lower cost per lead, and more appointment bookings. For Indian medical practices, the recommended campaign structure is:

### Campaign 1-Brand Protection

Always run a branded campaign targeting your clinic name and doctor name. Without it, competitors can bid on your name and steal patients searching specifically for you.

### Campaign 2-Specialty Services

Separate campaigns per specialty: Cardiology, Dermatology, Orthopaedics, Gynaecology, Paediatrics. Each specialty has distinct patient intent, different CPCs, and should have its own budget allocation.

### Campaign 3-Telehealth / Online Consultation

Online doctor consultations are a fast-growing search category in India. A dedicated campaign for "online consultation [specialty]" captures this high-intent segment with typically lower CPC than in-clinic keywords.

### Campaign 4-Call-Only Campaigns (Mobile)

India has over 750 million smartphone users. Call-only campaigns appear exclusively on mobile and drive direct phone calls-no landing page required. Ideal for urgent care, gynaecology emergency queries, and paediatric urgent care.

