**Budget Allocation Formula:**

> **Monthly Budget** = Target New Patients × Average Cost Per Lead
**Example:** 30 patients × ₹600 CPL = ₹18,000/month minimum
**Add 20% testing buffer** = ₹21,600 recommended starting budget

### Section 4-Landing Page + WhatsApp Integration Outline

This is where Indian medical practices have a decisive competitive advantage that no competitor's guide addresses. WhatsApp is the primary communication channel for appointment booking in India-integrating it into your Google Ads landing pages can increase conversions by 30–50% compared to form-only pages.

## Landing Page Structure for Indian Clinics:

1. **Above the Fold:** Headline matching ad copy + Click-to-Call button + WhatsApp Chat button (equally prominent)
1. **Trust Bar:** Google Reviews rating (minimum 4.5★), years of experience, certifications, clinic photos
1. **Service Section:** Specific treatment covered in the ad-not a full services list
1. **Appointment Options:** 3 clear paths-Call Now, WhatsApp Us, Book Online-patients choose their preferred channel
1. **Doctor Profile:** Photo, qualification (MBBS, MD, DNB), hospital affiliations-EEAT critical for YMYL healthcare content
1. **Patient Reviews:** Minimum 5 verified Google reviews embedded on page
1. **Compliance:** India's Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023 consent banner on all forms collecting patient data

### Section 5 — EEAT Outline for Indian Healthcare Content

Google classifies medical websites under **Your Money or Your Life (YMYL)** — the highest scrutiny category. A Google Ads for doctors SEO outline must ensure that both paid and organic efforts align — creating stronger Quality Scores and building patient trust simultaneously.

{% table %}
- EEAT Factor
- Implementation for Indian Practices
---
- **Experience**
- Years in practice, patient volume, conditions treated, clinical outcomes
---
- **Expertise**
- MBBS, MD, DNB, DM credentials prominently displayed on landing pages and blog author bio
---
- **Authoritativeness**
- Medical council registrations, hospital affiliations, media mentions, CME certifications
---
- **Trustworthiness**
- Verified Google reviews, DPDP Act compliance, SSL certificate, transparent fee display
{% /table %}

### Section 6-30-60-90 Day Action Roadmap

**No competing guide provides a structured timeline. Here is the exact sequence for Indian medical practices:**

#### Days 1–30 — Foundation

1. Keyword research completed, negative keyword list built (minimum 100 terms)
1. Campaign structure set up-one campaign per specialty
1. DPDP-compliant landing pages built per service
1. Call tracking + WhatsApp tracking + form submission tracking active
1. Google Business Profile fully optimized and linked to Google Ads
1. Manual CPC bidding-collect baseline data

#### Days 31–60-Optimization

1. Review Search Terms Report weekly-add negative keywords continuously
1. Identify top 20% of keywords driving 80% of conversions-increase bids Pause keywords spending budget without
1. generating leads A/B test: landing page headline variations, CTA button text, WhatsApp vs Call CTA placement Switch to
1. Target CPA bidding once 30+ conversions tracked

#### Days 61–90-Scale

1. Scale budget on winning campaigns-20–30% budget increase on profitable ad groups
1. Launch remarketing campaign-re-engage website visitors who did not book
1. Launch telehealth campaign layer if not already running
1. Begin SEO blog content targeting informational medical keywords
1. Connect paid keyword conversion data to SEO content strategy-publish blog posts targeting keywords your ads prove convert

### Section 7 — Seasonal & Festive Bidding Calendar for India

Indian patient search behavior has strong seasonal patterns that most practices — and all competitor guides — completely ignore:

{% table %}
- Period
- Search Spike
- Recommended Action
---
- **Jan–Feb (Winter)**
- Respiratory, orthopaedic
- Increase bids 15–20%
---
- **Apr–Jun (Summer)**
- Dermatology, dehydration, paediatric
- Increase bids 20–25%
---
- **Jul–Sep (Monsoon)**
- Vector-borne diseases, gastroenterology
- Surge bids for relevant specialties
---
- **Oct–Nov (Post-Festive)**
- Elective procedures, health checkups
- Cosmetic surgery, ophthalmology scale
---
- **Dec–Jan (Year End)**
- Health checkups, insurance utilization
- General physician, diagnostics peak
{% /table %}

Adjust your Google Ads bids 7–10 days before each seasonal peak — search volume builds before the actual season begins.

**Conclusion**

A comprehensive Google Ads for doctors SEO outline is not a one-time document-it is a living strategic framework that evolves as your campaign data grows, your SEO authority builds, and your patient acquisition system matures.

The practices growing fastest in Indian healthcare are not spending the most on Google Ads. They are spending the most strategically-with structured campaigns, India-specific keyword targeting, WhatsApp-integrated landing pages, seasonal bid adjustments, and real conversion data driving every optimization decision.
